From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:06:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: recheck flow state after winning the add work

The refresh path tests the closing and teardown bits before it wins
the pending bit. A teardown or a hardware delete that lands in
between leaves an add work queued on a flow that garbage collection
can release. It can also reinstall a hardware entry that nothing
removes.

The add path now tests the bits again once it holds the pending bit,
and backs off if any is set. All the bits live in one word, so either
the add path sees the teardown or garbage collection sees the pending
bit.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c |   12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -1147,6 +1147,18 @@ void nf_flow_offload_add(struct nf_flowt
 	if (!offload)
 		return;
 
+	/* The caller tested these bits before it won the pending bit; a
+	 * teardown or a hardware delete that landed in between must win,
+	 * or the work would run on a flow the gc is free to release.
+	 */
+	if (test_bit(NF_FLOW_TEARDOWN, &flow->flags) ||
+	    test_bit(NF_FLOW_CLOSING, &flow->flags) ||
+	    test_bit(NF_FLOW_HW_DYING, &flow->flags)) {
+		clear_bit_unlock(NF_FLOW_HW_PENDING, &flow->flags);
+		kfree(offload);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	flow_offload_queue_work(offload);
 }
 
